From 348b0c6dd5807d94ba3deed96fa9615308ec1c44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini experiment <experiment@invalid>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:36:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: request the re-arm from the station teardown in
 the stable epoch

The lifecycle boot ran one full lifetime (join, data phase, standard
disconnect, stage-3 cleanup with credits returned, keys removed) and then
logged nothing for the remaining eleven minutes: no re-arm, no refusal,
no fault. Proposal 0240 unlocked the re-arm for the stable epoch at the
worker's rendezvous site only, but no worker pass runs after a retired
terminal, and the other requester, the mac80211 station teardown, still
refused to queue the re-arm pass under the stable epoch and the old
two-lifetime cap. Drop both gates there and require the healthy stage-3
cleanup to be done already, so a teardown that arrives first cannot log a
false refusal and the worker's site keeps that order. The rendezvous,
quiescence and wrap rules of the re-arm pass are unchanged.

Internal experiment archive; synthetic non-certifying author,
not submission-ready.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c | 14 +++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c
index fbaebefa2..17ead811d 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c
@@ -5724,11 +5724,15 @@ static int mt6797_mac_sta_state(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 					 * the pass with sta_removed=false and log a false refusal.
 					 */
 					close = false;
-					if (mac->join_sta_removed && !mac->join_closed &&
-#ifdef CONFIG_MT6797_CCMP_STABLE_EPOCH
-					    !ccmp_stable_epoch &&
-#endif
-					    mac->join_lifetimes < 2 && !mac->join_rearm_pending) {
+					/* The stable epoch re-arms too (0240 unlocked the worker's
+					 * site only; no worker pass runs after a retired terminal,
+					 * so this teardown is the only requester once the healthy
+					 * stage-3 cleanup is already done). The cleanup_done test
+					 * keeps a teardown that precedes the terminal from logging
+					 * a false refusal; the worker's site then requests it.
+					 */
+					if (mac->join_sta_removed && mac->join_cleanup_done &&
+					    !mac->join_closed && !mac->join_rearm_pending) {
 						mac->join_rearm_pending = true;
 						schedule_delayed_work(&mac->join_work, 0);
 					}
